6. Go modules — compiled into the lens binary
--------------------------------------------

Lens is built from source (`make build`) into a single static binary. The
module sources are fetched from the Go module proxy at build time and are not
redistributed in this repository, but a built bin/lens contains the
following, each under its own licence (go.mod / go.sum pin the versions;
`go version -m bin/lens` lists exactly what a given binary links):

  golang.org/x/net, golang.org/x/text, golang.org/x/sys      BSD-3-Clause
                                              (Copyright The Go Authors)
  modernc.org/sqlite, modernc.org/libc, modernc.org/mathutil,
  modernc.org/memory                                          BSD-3-Clause
  github.com/google/uuid, github.com/remyoudompheng/bigfft    BSD-3-Clause
  github.com/dustin/go-humanize                               MIT

modernc.org/sqlite is the SQLite C library (public domain) translated to Go,
and modernc.org/libc carries code derived from musl libc (MIT) and the Go
standard library (BSD-3-Clause); both modules ship a LICENSE-3RD-PARTY.md
with the full notices. The Go standard library and runtime linked into every
Go binary are BSD-3-Clause (Copyright The Go Authors).

Anyone redistributing a built binary must carry these notices with it.


7. python-dotenv — ported (internal/dotenv)
-------------------------------------------

internal/dotenv/ is a Go port of python-dotenv 1.2.3
(https://github.com/theskumar/python-dotenv) — its parser, ${VAR}
interpolation and the parts of main.py Lens uses — together with test cases
ported from its test suite. It reads .env files with exactly the grammar the
Python release used:

