The ported files say so in their headers and remain under that licence as
well.


8. CPython html.parser — ported (internal/htmldom)
--------------------------------------------------

internal/htmldom/parser.go is a port of the tokenizer in CPython 3.12's
html.parser module, and internal/htmldom/entities.go is generated from
CPython's html.entities.html5 table (the WHATWG named character references).

  Copyright (c) 2001 Python Software Foundation; All Rights Reserved.
  Python Software Foundation License Version 2
  https://docs.python.org/3/license.html

The tree it builds reproduces the behaviour of Beautiful Soup 4.15.0's
html.parser tree builder (MIT); no Beautiful Soup code is included.


